=== C. S4 Cayley long-horizon drift  (outcome accuracy, seeds=10) ===
  Corrects the paper's '1.00 at any horizon': only the EXACT SYMBOLIC model (one-hot
  codes + regular embedding, built by construction) is truly drift-free; the LEARNED
  PreNat drifts at long horizon (its codes never lock exactly).
  model                              |h=1    h=5    h=10   h=40   h=100  h=200 
  SYMBOLIC (exact, by construction)  | 1.00  1.00  1.00  1.00  1.00  1.00 
  TransE                             | 0.07  0.04  0.04  0.04  0.04  0.04 
  RESCAL                             | 0.97  0.75  0.47  0.04  0.04  0.04 
  PreNat (learned)                   | 1.00  0.97  0.94  0.86  0.24  0.14 
  (per-horizon 95% CI at h=200):
    PreNat-learned h200: 0.139 [0.039,0.332]   RESCAL h200: 0.043 [0.039,0.047]   SYMBOLIC h200: 1.00
  HONEST READING: exactness/drift-freeness is a property of the SYMBOLIC algebra (a
  hand/discovery-committed lookup), NOT of the gradient-learned model; see
  discover_compose.py for the discovery->commit chain that earns it.

